  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its of its excessive depth, height, detailed design, bulk, and proximity to the side site boundary would result in an overly dominant and visually intrusive form of development which would have an adverse impact on character and appearance of the host building and would be detrimental to the visual amenities of the immediate area, including this part of the Bush Hill Park Conservation Area. The identified harm is not outweighed by any public benefits. The proposal is therefore contrary to Sections 12 and 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (2021), policies CP30 and CP31 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD11, DMD13, DMD37 and DMD44 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014),  the Bush Hill Conservation Area Management Proposals  (2015) and the Enfield Heritage Strategy 2019 - 2024 (2019).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its excessive depth, height and proximity to the side site boundary, would give rise to an unneighbourly and overly dominant form of development which would result in an unacceptable loss of sunlight, daylight and outlook, as perceived from the neighbouring property at No. 7 Private Road. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD11 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).\r"
  ],
